title: 'cumulus: fix best parent selection when the build parent re-derives the relay chain context'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    When the build parent's scheduling params disagree with the para best head's, the
    slot-based collator re-derives the relay chain context from the parent — but kept the
    parent found under the old context unconditionally, even when it is invalid under the
    new one (V2: relay parent outside the allowed ancestry after a relay chain fork, V3: no
    longer backable at the new scheduling parent). The re-derivation now re-validates the
    parent under the new context and falls back to the pending/included block when the
    check fails; the included-header snapshot likewise follows the settled context.
    `cumulus-client-consensus-common` exposes the pieces the re-check needs:
    `search_start_block` and `is_parent_valid_for_params`, sharing the parent search's own
    validity rule.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
  bump: minor
